    "https://www.military.com/veteran-jobs/career-advice": {
      "title": "Career Advice",
      "description": "Career Advice | Military.com Insurance Mortgages VA Loans Check VA Loan Rates Money HomeFront Grant Credit Cards Personal Finance Military Pay Information Military Pay Charts Join the Military Contact a Recruiter ASVAB Navy Advancement Benefits Military Pay and Benefits GI Bill Veteran Health Care Tricare Retirement Discounts News Army Navy Air Force Marine Corps Coast Guard Space Force Military Life Military Base Guides Veteran Jobs Military Transition Off Duty Games Auto Fitness Daily Trivia Game Spouse & Family Military History Login Insurance Mortgages VA Loans Check VA Loan Rates Money HomeFront Grant Credit Cards Personal Finance Military Pay Information Military Pay Charts Join the Military Contact a Recruiter ASVAB Navy Advancement Benefits Military Pay and Benefits GI Bill Veteran Health Care Tricare Retirement Discounts News Army Navy Air Force Marine Corps Coast Guard Space Force Military Life Military Base Guides Veteran Jobs Military Transition Off Duty Games Auto Fitness Daily Trivia Game Spouse & Family Military History Sign in Newsletter Insurance VA Loan Recruiter Close Career Advice Whether you are transitioning to the civilian workplace or simply want to know what interview questions to prepare for, find career advice and tips here. + See More The Soldier for Life and U.S. Army Partnership for Your Success Program teams attend the Military Influencer Conference in Atlanta, GA, September 22-24, 2025.(Photo by Melani Harig, DVIDS) Related Companies with Supportive Veteran Cultures To support the long-term success of a veteran employee, companies with great veteran culture operationalize it with visible outcomes. Posts (Adobe stock image) Related 8 High-Powered Jobs for Leaders After the Military The fact is that the leadership gene that steered you into the military and kept you here so long is one of your best, most marketable traits. Posts (Adobe stock image) Related Civilian Jobs that Sound So Wrong But Could Be So Right for Veterans Even though military job seekers long for security, staying loose at the first set of offers can allow you more time to learn about the company, the work and what you truly want. Posts Harold Little, right, a retired Navy lieutenant, exchanges paperwork with a company representative during a large-scale military job fair in Ponte Vedra Beach, Florida, May 2, 2015. (Sgt. 1st Class Tyrone C. Marshall Jr./U.S. Army photo) Related How to Avoid Underselling Yourself During a Job Search In a world where everyone seems loud and life is moving at warp speed, it’s easy to blend in and miss the opportunity to showcase your value. Posts (Ryan White/U.S. Air Force photo) Related Government Jobs: Cracking the GS Code Federal job classification systems vary by agency, but the most widely used is the General Schedule (GS), which covers most civilian white-collar positions. Most federal employees must be U.S. citizens or nationals, though limited exceptions exist under s Posts Free Veteran Employment Master Classes (Adobe stock image) Related Iron Sharpens Iron: New Master Class Teaches How to Find the Mentor You Need on the Job Hunt The best and brightest tool in your transition toolkit is a well-placed mentor who can show you where your military experience meets market demand. In this transition master class, learn to activate past mentors, identify mentorship opportunities in veter Posts (Adobe stock image) Related Master Class: How Female Veterans Can Land a Job with a 6-Figure Income Faster Female military members do the same work as male military members, but they find a much different outcome on the civilian job market. How can female veterans overcome some of these invisible, unfathomable barriers to employment and land desirable jobs, es Posts (Adobe stock image) Related Master Class: How to Be a Project Manager Being a project manager is a natural role for a veteran or military spouse. Your ability to see what needs to be done, organize and lead groups, work with time constraints, and scheme around limited resources can lead to success in a new career. Find out Posts (Adobe stock image) Related Defense Jobs Master Class: Use Your Military Skills to Get Your Dream Job During Military Transition Military to civilian job seekers are facing an ever-tightening job market. You need to be more strategic, more adaptable and much more knowledgeable about how the employment game is played, especially when it comes to jobs in the defense industry. Our Def Posts Related The New Resume Essentials No One Else Knows: Checklist Resume Master Class 2025 Now that artificial intelligence (AI) tools can do so much of the work of building a resume, what else is there for a veteran or military spouse job seeker to learn? Posts Taking ideas from resumes in books or online galleries can greatly improve your own. (Adobe stock image) Related How to Know When Your Resume Is ‘Ready’ Here are some understandings about the role of the resume to help you determine whether yours is ready to send. Posts The Army Community Service Employment Readiness Program assists military-connected job seekers in federal employment, including account creation, hiring eligibility and resume tailoring, promoting a 5-page federal resume. (Illustration by Jason Ragucci/Fort Liberty Garrison Public Affairs Office) Related How to Write the Right Federal Resume When it comes to a federal resume, the rules are different, and to ignore these rules is to risk not getting referred. Posts Close Career Advice Headlines 4 Tips to Help You Choose a Career Path Veteran Jobs One day you're interested in aerospace careers and the next day you think a career in law enforcement would be cool. The following day, you lean towards defense contracting, and the day after that you swing way back to your fascination with mechanics Posts By MLT Staff Transition Noise: Why You Should Stop Listening to Everyone — Almost Veteran Jobs As you enter the transition phase of your career, refer to this list to help you stay open yet grounded. Posts By Lida  Citroen The Next Skilled Trades Workforce Revolution Will Be Veteran-Led Veteran Veterans create one of the largest skilled workforce pipelines into safety, infrastructure, firearms and UAS operations. Posts By Kimberly O'Brien Veteran Job-Hunters: Sharpen Your 'Soft Skills' to Gain an Edge Veteran Jobs In the civilian sector, your military skills are still important, but your soft skills are also highly desired. Posts By Lida  Citroen Why Approachability Matters for Veterans Veteran Jobs Being approachable means others feel a degree of psychological safety around you. They can share their hopes, fears, concerns and ideas without fear of retribution, ridicule or consequences. Posts By Lida  Citroen Email or DM? How to Communicate Clearly and Confidently in Online Job Networking Veteran Jobs As if job fairs, networking events and coffee chats weren’t tricky enough, now we must network online, too. Posts By Lida  Citroen Is That Job Posting Real? 10 Ways to Spot a Scam Veteran Jobs As more people seek remote, work-from-home jobs, the chances of being scammed by an illegitimate posting have increased. Here’s what to look out for. Posts By Lida  Citroen Shortages Lead to Higher Pay in the Civilian Aviation Industry Military Transition Global shortages of aircraft mechanics and commercial airline pilots could translate to civilian career opportunities for members of the military. Posts By Amanda Miller Can You Make a Living Working for a Nonprofit? Career Advice If you feel a strong desire to continue serving after leaving the military, but fear that working for a charity or nonprofit could make it hard to support your family, you’re not alone. Posts By Lida  Citroen 5 Stories Every Veteran Should Be Sharing Military Transition Civilian employers value effective storytellers who convey experience in ways that resonate beyond business or military jargon. Posts By Lida  Citroen How to Back Out of an Argument in the Workplace Military Transition Arguments are never pleasant. Self-control, self-awareness and empathy are proven ways to get yourself out of an argument, especially at work. Posts By Lida  Citroen Why You Didn’t Get the Job: Understanding How Companies Hire Veteran Jobs In today’s turbulent, unpredictable and frustrating hiring market, job-seekers are seemingly doing everything right and sometimes not landing a role. Posts By Lida  Citroen Underemployed After the Military? Here’s How to Fix It Military Transition When it’s time to transition to the civilian sector, fears of underemployment can loom large as you recognize that your work thus far doesn’t map cleanly to a private-sector career path. Posts By MLT Staff Continued Health Care Benefit Program Overview Veterans Health Care Temporary health insurance is available after you get out of the military. You can buy up to 18 months of temporary coverage. Posts By Amanda Miller Should You Sell Back Leave or Take Terminal Leave When You Get Out? Military Transition In the final months of active duty, one of the biggest decisions isn’t about paperwork or moving logistics — it’s whether to take terminal leave or sell it. Posts By MLT Staff Reset Your Job Search Mindset for the New Calendar Year Veteran Jobs As you turn the page on the calendar, prepare for a fresh new start in your job search with these tips: Posts By Lida  Citroen Career Advice: How to Defend Your Position Without Being Defensive Veteran Jobs Since your reaction to a situation, comment or person is completely up to you, it’s important to get this right. Posts By Lida  Citroen How to Navigate Civilian Coworkers’ Ignorance About Your Military Service Veteran Jobs By definition, ignorance means a lack of knowledge, information or education. It can refer to a general lack of knowledge or be specific to a particular subject and is distinct from stupidity, as it implies a lack of information rather than an inability t Posts By Lida  Citroen Famous Veteran: Kris Kristofferson Famous Veterans Country music legend and Army veteran Kris Kristofferson has a list of accomplishments so long, it might be faster to list off things he hasn't done. Posts By Blake Stilwell Famous Veteran: Bob Ross Famous Veterans Bob Ross was probably the nicest person who ever lived, and it showed through in his work. Most of America knows him as the host of the long-running show \"The Joy of Painting,\" but a select few know him better as an Air Force military training i Posts By Blake Stilwell See More Veteran Job Topics Veteran Jobs Veteran Employment Project Vet Friendly Employers Career Advice Military Transition Hiring Veterans Job Fairs Get The Military.com Newsletter Stay connected to your community and take full advantage of the Military.com experience by subscribing to the newsletter. Subscribe Now By signing up, you agree to receive newsletter and marketing emails, and accept our Terms of Use and Privacy Policy . You can unsubscribe anytime. Select a Service Army Marines Navy Air Force Space Force Coast Guard National Guard Spouse Log in Trending Now The Best Military Discounts for Football Season Widow of Airman Killed in Iran War Claims She Was Denied Death Benefits Veterans to Safeguard Polling Places Against Potential Intimidation During Midterm Elections GO → Mortgages VA Loans Check VA Loan Rates Money HomeFront Grant Credit Cards Personal Finance Military Pay Information Military Pay Charts Join the Military Contact a Recruiter ASVAB Navy Advancement Benefits Military Pay and Benefits GI Bill Veteran Health Care Tricare Retirement Discounts News Army Navy Air Force Marine Corps Coast Guard Space Force Military Life Military Base Guides Veteran Jobs Military Transition Off Duty Games Auto Fitness Daily Trivia Game Spouse & Family Military History Resources Insurance Military.com Network Air Force Army Coast Guard Marine Corps Navy Space Force About Military.com About Us & Press Room Newsletter Contact Us Advertise with Us User Agreement Privacy Policy Your Privacy Choices RSS Site Map Need customer support? Visit our Customer Support center for solutions or to contact us. Customer Support"
